<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Putins War Threading the Needle, 2022</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Putins War Threading the Needle, 2020&lt;BR&gt;The Time Is: 5 June 2020, 23:00 UTC / 6 June 2020, 00:00 Stockholm Time&lt;BR&gt;Near &lt;BR&gt;Playable as Russia only&lt;BR&gt;Up to a 16 Hours Duration&lt;BR&gt;This is a very small but challenging scenario&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;The Russian cyber-attack on the Baltic States on Saturday, May 28th succeeded far beyond all expectations! Within hours the banking systems of Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania completely collapsed as did much of the power grid and governmental functions. On Sunday (May 29th), the attack spread to telecommunications and a general denial of service attack on the internet system itself.&amp;nbsp; As the attacks occurred over the weekend people generally took them in stride treating the disruptions as a holiday, but on Monday (May 30th) when the majority of people tried to return to work chaos reigned. Street lights and street cars wouldn’t function, commercial transactions were impossible and the eastern portion of each country remained in the dark.&amp;nbsp; By that evening, the mood had turned bitter with young people lingering and drinking in the streets and public parks.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;On Tuesday the 31st violent disturbances broke out in Navra, Tartu and Rezekne with young Russian men clashing with police. As the crisis entered its fifth day, on Wednesday (June 1st), the Prime Minister of Latvia was shot and killed by an assassin while visiting the town of Balvi. By Thursday, June 2nd, full scale food riots had broken out across all three countries and, blaming Russia, fighting between ethnic Russians and Latvians became intense in the eastern portion of the country. Up until this point Russian President Vladimr Putun had been very silent on the Baltic developments, but he now called for “Volunteers” to aide their beleaguered and oppressed fellow ethnic Russians.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;As chaos continued to descend upon the Baltic all three nations jointly invoked NATO Article Five asking Brussels for aide. Debate raged in NATO General Council during the late week (June 1st and 2nd) until it was proven on Friday (June 3rd) that “Little Green Men” were appearing more and more frequently in the growing civil unrest. Late that day, NATO authorized support for the Baltic Republics and that night a British Tornado air strike destroyed a convoy of “volunteers” crossing the Russian border near Luta, Estonia. Saturday afternoon (the 4th), it became a free for all over the skies of the Baltics with NATO and Russian Jets mixing it up over the border area and several NATO aircraft were downed by Russian SA-400 missile batteries. To date, the crisis had been confined to the Baltic States but at 18:00 UTC a French satellite pass noted the Russian SSBNs getting underway from the Kola Peninsula and other satellite passes confirmed the rest of the Northern and Baltic Fleets getting ready to stand up…&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Designer’s Notes:&lt;BR&gt;1. In 2019 Sweden reactivated the Muskö Naval Base on the island of Muskö just south of Stockholm. The base, built during the Cold War, has three dock facilities and miles of underground tunnels, magazines and machine shops. Vessels of the Swedish 4th Naval Warfare Flotilla, and it is rumored some NATO units, began to base out of the newly activated base. Your mission is to scout the base, prior to the outbreak of hostilities.&lt;BR&gt;2. Your Submarine must either remain in the Kilo Box (the bay) for four (4) hours or the Musko Naval Base Box for five minutes (getting there will likely take you bout two [2] to three [3] hours of game time) to win. In either case you will have been considered to have gained enough intelligence to have succeeded in your mission.&lt;BR&gt;3. The channel into the base winds and is very shallow on both sides, it will take all of your navigational skills to survive.&lt;BR&gt;4. Civilian vessels are initially set to a “Hostile” posture, I suggest as you ID them you mark as neutral.&lt;BR&gt;5. Sweden is hostile to you; they take a dim view of Russian submarines in their territorial waters. They will fire on you when they detect and classify you. If they look like they are taking an attack posture destroy them to preserve your command, but if moving away do not provoke them.&lt;BR&gt;6. This is a very binary scenario, you either win or you lose. I did add some points for sinking Swedish vessels but it is not your primary function.&lt;BR&gt;7. The longer this mission takes the more chance you will encounter ASW Helicopters.&lt;BR&gt;8. At 00:00 utc June 6th, Russian ground forces will attack into the Baltic States and at 00:00 on June 7th military action will begin against Scandinavia (including “neutral” Finland and Sweden) so this is a pre-conflict scouting mission.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1.01 Build 1134.1 – Data Base: DB3000 483&lt;BR&gt;An .INI and Delta File have both been provided for rebuilds&lt;BR&gt;Al “BeirutDude” Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;BR&gt;&lt;A href="mailto:Al.Sandrik@gmail.com"&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/A&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
